{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1136833-summer-glamour-and-banality","id":1136833,"title":"Summer, Glamour and Banality","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-02T22:22:10-07:00","id":1136833,"title":"Summer, Glamour and Banality","content":"I'm not sure if I'm the only one, but...<br /> From reading the setting on C20, one gets the impression that Glamour is getting even more scarce and Banality is a greater threat than it was during 1st or 2nd ed. However, when you get to the systems, it doesn't seem that way. Now, although i find personal Banality triggers are an awesome idea, it seems as if everytime you would have earned a point of Banality, you get now a roll to avoid gaining it. Even worse, Summer levels 4 and 5 let you regain Glamour and burn off Permanent Banality (yes, it causes damage, and hurts awfully, but you can use healing magic and be right as rain on the next turn...)<br /> <br /> Has anyone come up with a house-rule or alternative Summer levels?<br /> Am I alone in thinking this kinda defeats the sense of danger and dread Banality is supposed to engender in Kithain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T01:34:41-07:00","id":1136858,"title":"","content":"Well in previous editions, atleast in my personal opinion, Glamour was scarce enough that players were often unable to use any ability that required Glamour as a cost, and thus build characters in a manner that they wouldnt need to. This went at toimea so far as to players almost never using Arts as they often cost Glamour for them. Basically many of my players nearly ignored half the system if possible just to avoid spending Glamour. Similarly Banality was and still is a horridly dangerous to any Changeling.<br /> <br /> One of the objectives of C20 was to remain true to the concept of scarce Glamour but still making it available enough to make the game more playable as scarcity of Glamour has been one of the greatest complain about Changeling over the years. So in this editions they have scale down some of the costs from birthrights for example, I used to House rule almost all the birthright costs away in previous editions since I actually wanted people to use them, and gave us a few new ways to gain Glamour. Really things were vad enough that Pooka rarely if ever use their shapechange as it cost them apoint of precious Glamour but now Pooka can shapechange for free if alone which makes all the difference, as far as playability is concerned.<br /> <br /> Banality on the other hand remains, again in my opinion at least, a threat to every Kithain out there. Yes now there is a trigger roll to gain Banality and while it can mean that at times you are able to avoid gaining a point of Banality it also means there is always a risk of gaining several points as well, since we all botch rolls at times and sometimes the dice can get downright hostile.<br /> <br /> Now as for the summer cantrips.<br /> While I agree that Vestas Blessing is a powerful Cantrip it does require considerable investment in Summer, and thus isn't something always awailable, without Unleashing Summer of course but that can get rather interesting. But while powerful it is but one of the added means to gain Glamour and thus make the game more enjoyable, again YMMV, and is not atleast in my eyes in any way overpowered. It doesn't make Summer into something must have but it is a nice ability to have for those times when all seem lost and players are trying to recover from a climatic encounter that has drained their willpower and Glamour pools, I could even see it as a convenient ST tool that allows game to more on a bit faster after such an encounter without players necessarily needing to take a few weeks to rest and recuperate.<br /> <br /> And as for the Beltaine Blade... well first of all it removes Banality points not dots ergo it does nothing to your permanent Banality score and it only does even that if you roll 5+ to activate it and then strike someone with aggravated damage and should they even survive such a strike, you could rather easily kill a fellow player trying this, you would loose at best 3 points of Banality and have 6 points of aggravated damage to heal. Hurts like hell, has a very real risk of death, and only removes points of Banality. Seems balanced to me and doesnt really take the teeth away from Banality in my eyes at least.<br /> <br /> Of course these opinions can vary from people to people but I for one find that the changes made for Glamour and Banality in C20 have just made the game stronger and better overall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T23:09:46-07:00","id":1137927,"title":"","content":"Isn't the best way to remove temporary Banaliy is to regain temporary Glamour to trade it 1-to-1 as per rules (Removing Banality; p. 174. C20), which makes The Beltaine Blade a bit redundant (and extremely discouraged) for that goal?<br /> <br /> It's great offensive Cantrip, though.<br /> <br /> And yes, you may notice the distinction: The Beltaine Blade refers to &quot;points&quot; of Banility, temporary one, while permanent Banality is measured with &quot;dots&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 09-07-2017, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T19:06:48-07:00","id":1139330,"title":"","content":"Isn't the expenditure of Glamour to counter Banality only used when you gain new Banality?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T21:04:41-07:00","id":1139345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luisarmander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1136833-summer-glamour-and-banality?p=1139330#post1139330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't the expenditure of Glamour to counter Banality only used when you gain new Banality?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the other way around. Everytime you gain Glamour you have the option to remove a point of Banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T20:03:33-07:00","id":1140405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1136833-summer-glamour-and-banality?p=1139345#post1139345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the other way around. Everytime you gain Glamour you have the option to remove a point of Banality.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it has been that way in previous versions of the game as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}